/-! # Ordinary tower inverse-image tensor constraints

Source: Stacks 03EL, 07A4 and the tensor-map argument of
`literature/blueprint/latest/blueprint/sec-smooth-purity/sk-prop-sp-purity-bc/
sk-prop-sp-purity-bc-factors.proof.md`, (2).
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section
set_option autoImplicit false
set_option synthInstance.maxSize 4096
universe u
open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.MonoidalCategory AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme
namespace AlgebraicGeometry.ProEtale.CtfPullbackConstraints
variable (ell : ℕ) [Fact ell.Prime] (E : Type u) [Field E]
  [Algebra (Padic ell) E] [FiniteDimensional (Padic ell) E]
  (b : SpTowerShriek.Base ell E) (o : SpTowerShriek.Operations ell E b)

/-- Ordinary system inverse image carries the regular coefficient module to the
regular coefficient module, independently of derived tensor constraints.
Source: Stacks 03EL, 07A4; factors proof (2), coefficient identification.
(blueprint: lem-sp-tower-pullback-coefficient-object).

Proof: at level n use the ringUnderlying and moduleUnderlying comparisons of the
retained algebraic inverse image to identify the image of the regular module with
the target regular module. Both actions are multiplication and the map sends the
unit to the unit. The coefficient_compatibility equation and ordinaryPullTransition
show that these isomorphisms commute with every quotient transition, so they form
an ordinary system isomorphism; use the retained coordinate equalities to put it
in the fixed constant-ring coordinates. This gives the ordinary system
isomorphism, without taking any derived evaluation. Empty schemes and zero
quotient rings use the same regular-module construction. No tensor coherence
is assumed. -/
theorem tower_pullback_coefficient_object {S T : Scheme.{u}} (g : T ⟶ S) :
    Nonempty (((o.geometry g).pull).obj
      (SpTowerClasses.coefficient S (SpTowerClasses.Arings ell E S)) ≅
        SpTowerClasses.coefficient T (SpTowerClasses.Arings ell E T)) := by sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.ProEtale.CtfPullbackConstraints
